Feature: Batteries, airframes and the loadout
  In the [[v4 rules]], a team has a fixed number of airframes, and it chooses them before the game.
  A drone that lands at its base for a [[battery swap]] gets a full battery in 30 s. A drone that
  only circles over its base recharges, but slowly. A drone that goes down is lost, and a spare
  takes its place. A team with no spare flies with fewer drones.

  Before the game, each commander chooses the [[loadout]] of the team: the airframes and their
  payloads. The first five fly at the start, and the rest are spares. The loadout costs points
  from a budget of 20. A light drone costs 2, a standard drone 3 and a heavy drone 4.

  Expectation: A drone that lands is on the ground at its base
    LAND sends a drone to its base. It lands there, and it stays on the ground until the commander
    gives it a new order.

    Given the battery swap is on
    And the first Blue drone is over its base
    When the first Blue drone lands at its base
    Then the condition of the first Blue drone is on the ground
    And the first Blue drone is at its base

  Expectation: A drone that lands at its base gets a full battery after 30 s
    Given the battery swap is on
    And the first Blue drone is at its base
    When the game runs for 30 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 240 s

  Expectation: A swap is not done before 30 s on the ground
    Overrides: A drone that lands at its base gets a full battery after 30 s
    The ground crew changes the whole battery, or none of it.

    Given the battery swap is on
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 50 s
    And the first Blue drone is at its base
    When the game runs for 20 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 50 s

  Expectation: A drone that circles over its base recharges 4 s each second
    Overrides: A drone over its base recharges 10 s each second
    The swap is the better trade, but a drone does not have to land. The drone still uses 1 s each
    second to fly, so it gains 3 s each second.

    Given the batteries are on
    And the battery swap is on
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 100 s
    And the first Blue drone is over its base
    When the first Blue drone circles over its base for 25 seconds
    Then the battery of the first Blue drone is 175 s

  Expectation: A spare takes the place of a drone that is lost
    Given the airframes are finite
    And the spares of Blue are 1
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 5 s
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the game runs for 40 seconds
    Then the condition of the first Blue drone is on the ground
    And the spares of Blue are 0

  Expectation: A team with no spare flies with fewer drones
    Overrides: A spare takes the place of a drone that is lost
    Overrides: A drone with an empty battery is down

    Given the airframes are finite
    And the spares of Blue are 0
    And the battery of the first Blue drone is 5 s
    And the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    When the game runs for 90 seconds
    Then the condition of the first Blue drone is down

  Expectation: A loadout costs no more than the budget
    Today's squad (three standard drones, a heavy and a light drone) costs 15. Two light spares
    make it 19.

    Given the loadout of Blue is today's squad and two light spares
    Then the cost of the Blue loadout is within the budget

  Expectation: A loadout over the budget is refused
    Overrides: A loadout costs no more than the budget
    The cost of seven standard drones is 21.

    Given the loadout of Blue is seven standard drones
    Then the cost of the Blue loadout is over the budget
